# Per-run test, profiling, and dev-server artifacts.
# sdk/ and assets/vendor/ are still tracked deliberately, so a fresh clone
# builds with zero external fetches -- but the built exes themselves are NOT:
# they used to be committed (every "Rebuild the release exe" commit re-added
# ~10MB), which only bloated history forever without being diffable. Build
# them locally with build.ps1 instead.
out/prof/
out/results/
out/corpus/
out/dev-certs/
out/dev-profile/
out/pasted-image-*.png
out/*.log
out/*.json
out/MDView.exe
out/MDView.debug.exe

# Build intermediates (the .res is 4.6 MB of re-embedded assets). PDBs are
# regenerable locally via build.ps1 and were never wanted in the shipped
# artifact in the first place -- keeping them out of history avoids
# repeatedly committing several MB of debug symbols on every rebuild.
*.res
*.obj
*.ilk
*.exp
*.pdb
out/test-textio.exe

# Node
node_modules/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# tools/bench/run.mjs's per-run history -- real wall-clock timing, specific
# to whatever machine ran it, so not meaningful to compare across different
# hardware or commit to shared history. tools/bench/baseline.json (the
# single promoted reference point tools/bench/compare.mjs actually checks
# against) is NOT excluded here -- that one is deliberately committed.
tools/bench/history/*.json

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
